  "purpose": "The AlmaLinux 10 repository metadata and keys the almalinux10-server-amd64 profile is built from. almalinux-repo-pinned.sh refuses a repository whose repomd.xml no longer has the sha256 recorded here, and a key file whose sha256 differs.",
  "basis": "Each repomd.xml was read by an anonymous HTTPS GET at the recorded time; the primary metadata it names was retained and verified against its checksum and open-checksum. AlmaLinux and EPEL do not sign repomd.xml, so the sha256 is what binds the metadata; every package is checked against the key. AlmaLinux publishes its updates into the minor tree it names, so a pin holds until the next push to that tree and is then re-pinned (toolchain/almalinux10/relock-almalinux.py), never loosened.",
